# The ruling: a single creature with lifelink dealing combat damage to several creatures at the same time causes one
# life-gaining event (CR 510.2, 702.15b, 119.9), so Leonardo's last ability triggers once. On turn 5 Leonardo (1/1) attacks
# unblocked and his lifelink grows him to a 2/2. On turn 7 Bot2 blocks him with Llanowar Elves and Ornithopter, and Bot1
# divides his 2 damage, 1 to each: Bot1 gains 2 in one event and Leonardo gets one counter (a 3/3 with two counters), not
# two. The Elves die; the Ornithopter (0/2) and Leonardo each keep 1 damage.

[Bot1 Deck]
Plains
Leonardo, Cutting Edge
Plains x18

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Ornithopter
Forest x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Hand.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains#2.Activate
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Leonardo, Cutting Edge > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
? Bot1.Life = 21
[T7 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Leonardo, Cutting Edge > Bot2)
[T7 Bot1.DeclareBlockers]
Bot2.Block(Llanowar Elves > Leonardo, Cutting Edge; Ornithopter > Leonardo, Cutting Edge)
Bot1.AssignDamage(Leonardo, Cutting Edge > Llanowar Elves: 1; Leonardo, Cutting Edge > Ornithopter: 1)
[T7 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Life = 23
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Leonardo, Cutting Edge.Damage = 1
Bot2.Graveyard = Llanowar Elves
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Damage = 1
